# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXAONE Tabular (LG AI Research): both tasks, query rows AND context rows, from the published safetensors.
#
# Like Causilo / LimiX the context rows come from a second pass (the context presented again as queries).
# The model standardises its own features and the wrapper standardises the regression target in-graph and
# reduces the 999-quantile head to its mean, so the engine does neither (profile exaone_v1_raw).
#
# Parity with upstream's own single forward (float32 CPU) is exercised out-of-band
# (tools/export_exaone/tests/test_real_weights.py, docs/REAL_MODELS.md): through the built-in path iris 45/45
# and wine 54/54 query labels identical, diabetes within 1.7e-4 (target std 71), california_housing (1000-row
# sample) within 2.6e-5. It is a SINGLE forward, not upstream's 8-member ensemble.
#
# Measured on these tables (CPU): shared split accuracy 0.953 and query R2 0.99998; sep_t context and query
# 1.000; reg_t context corr 0.999997, query corr(yhat, f1) 0.9993 (predictions 59.1..67.6 where the truth
# reaches 72.3); reg_in query corr 0.999997, worst error 0.09. fitted_t is NOT asserted for this model: its
# label (i % 3) is not learnable from its features by EXAONE, and upstream's own eager forward answers one
# class for every row there too (probabilities within 0.34 / 0.33 / 0.33).

